provided an explanation of the termination clause contained in the agreement.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Williams voting “no”.
(#6376)
[CA]
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Public Works Department,
and United Way of Laramie County for Technical Assistance to Human Services Community
Programs (2015-2018 1% Sales Tax).  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried (amount not to exceed
$500,000.00 (2 year agreement in the amount of $250,000.00 annually)). (#6377)
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Cheyenne Airport Board for land to be used
for the Weed and Pest Division (2015-2018 1% Sales Tax).  Mr. Brown moved to approve in an
amount not to exceed $15,000.00 (4 year agreement in the amount of $3,750.00 annually), seconded
by Mr. Valdez.  Comments followed on leasing the property vs. locating City-owned property and
constructing a building for the Weed and Pest Division and affiliated cost, and community services
provided by the Division, which is not a revenue generating Division.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes”
-- all members of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Williams voting “no”. (#6378)
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Cheyenne Airport Board for land to be used
for the Street and Alley and Compost Divisions (2015-2018 1% Sales Tax).  Mr. Brown moved to
approve in an amount not to exceed $131,248.00 (4 year agreement in the amount of $32,812.00
annually), seconded by Mr. Roybal.  In response to inquiry, Mayor Kaysen advised finding a
different location for current operations at the leased site would be cost prohibitive based on the size
of area needed and distance from businesses/residences, and provided information on the mobile
trailer and porta-potties on site for employee accommodations.  Upon inquiry, Vicki Nemecek,
Public Works Director, provided further information on year ‘round composting operations; use of
port-potties for employees as there is no existing sanitary sewer system in the nearby area, and non-
ADA accommodation issues as customer service is provided outside at customers’ vehicles.  Motion
carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Williams
voting “no”.  (#6379)
[CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Cheyenne Airport Board for land to be used
for Parks and Recreation softball and baseball fields (2015-2018 1% Sales Tax).  Motion (per
