Under other business, Ms. Williams expressed concerns involving the women’s rest room
facilities at the Converse softball field; drainage issues at West Leisher and Stanfield, and reported
on a complaint she had received from a resident involving curb and gutter installation.  In response
to comments, Todd Feezer, Assistant Director, Parks and Recreation Department, noted he would
follow up on the concerns regarding the rest rooms; Nathan Beauheim, Acting City Engineer,
advised staff is reviewing the West Leisher/Stanfield site to determine the feasibility of potential
improvements, and Mayor Kaysen noted he was aware of the complaint involving curb and gutter
installation.
